        "left_mn7V8h": {
          "settings": {
            "dsc1": "<ul><li><strong>Wondering \"why do I have to suffer from painful cramps every month?\"</strong></li></ul><p>Period pain, also known as dysmenorrhea, is normally caused by prostaglandins - hormone-like chemicals found all over the body. The prostaglandins in the female reproductive tract help to regulate ovulation, menstruation, and labour. Prostaglandins cause the muscles of the uterus to contract - and this causes the pain you experience just before, and during your period. Those who have more prostaglandins usually experience more period pain. <strong>You can lower it by supporting your body with nutrient supplementation, diet and lifestyle changes, improving your period pain for good! </strong> </p><p></p><ul><li><strong>Factors Contributing:</strong> </li></ul><p>In today’s world, we are faced with heightened stress, hormone-disrupting chemicals, and nutrient-depleted food - f<strong>actors that can contribute to hormonal imbalances causing period pain and related symptoms </strong>such as cramps, bloating, mood swings, low energy, etc. </p><p>When pain begins, it's often too late to act naturally; which is why women have traditionally turned to painkillers that offer <strong>only</strong> temporary relief. </p><p><strong>We, however, refuse to accept that women should rely on quick fixes for life—or that menstrual pain should be seen as \"normal</strong>\". Our goal was to create a natural solution that addresses the root causes, offering long-term relief and empowering women to take control of their cycle and invest in their next period. </p><p>Created by five female doctors and women’s health professionals after personally helping over 2,500 women escape period pain at their clinics, monthlies brings together 26 of the most advanced natural ingredients to help tackle period cramps, replenish nutrient stores, support hormonal balance, and promote overall well-being.</p>"
